message.content:
Fix two components in this Next.js marketing site at /Users/yashbaldha/Desktop/Boldteq App/Marketing Site/Boldteq:

## Fix 1: Contact Hero — Change from dark to light blue background

**File:** src/components/contact/contact-hero.module.css

**Current .section class:**
```css
.section {
  background-color: #fff;
  background-image: url('/images/webflow/hero-background-1.png'), linear-gradient(#019ae614, #019ae600);
  background-position: 50% 100%, 0 0;
  background-repeat: no-repeat, repeat;
  background-size: cover, auto;
  padding-top: 4rem;
  padding-bottom: 4rem;
  position: relative;
}
```

**Webflow (.contact-banner):**
```css
background-color: #effafe;  /* light blue, NO image */
padding-top: 4rem;
padding-bottom: 6rem;       /* 6rem not 4rem */
```

Change:
- Remove background-image entirely
- Set `background-color: #effafe`
- Change padding-bottom from 4rem to 6rem
- Remove position: relative (or keep if needed by gradientFade child)

Also in contact-hero.module.css: Check if `.heading` has `color: #fff` — if so, change to `color: #082753`. Same for `.subtitle` — if white, change to `color: #2b2b2b`. If `.badge` or `.badgeText` has white text, change to dark colors appropriate for a light background: badge bg to rgba(33,207,255,0.1), border #05bafe, text #082753.

**File:** src/components/contact/contact-hero.tsx

The section is light blue now, so update the gradientFade div to fade from #effafe to transparent (or remove it). Also verify the heading and subtitle elements have appropriate class names and the text content matches Webflow: h1 = "Need any help? Contact us", subtitle = "Full-service agency crafting digital experiences that leave a lasting impression."

## Fix 2: Testimonials Grid Section — Fix background and padding

**File:** src/components/testimonials/testimonials-grid.module.css

**Current .section:**
```css
background-color: #f5f7fa; padding: 64px 5% 80px;
```

**Webflow (.work-sec2):**
```css
background-color: #fff;
padding: 220px 5% 64px;
position: relative;
```

Change `.section` to: `background-color: #fff; padding: 220px 5% 64px; position: relative;`

**Also check testimonials hero:** Read src/components/testimonials/testimonials-hero.tsx. If it's a dark-background hero section (like blog-hero), we need to remove it from the page OR make it transparent. Check src/app/testimonials/page.tsx - if TestimonialsHero is imported and rendered, comment it out since the 220px top padding of the grid section replaces the visual hero effect. But first read what testimonials-hero.tsx actually renders.

Read all files before editing.

